field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c865c2be-4f2c-573a-8a7d-ef0e3fdb4dd1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-447f87f9-dffa-5f29-8806-d225d659ee36" "answer-e692f2d1-6ddc-5aa1-9d7c-917bbfff6ebb" "answer-622f3578-83a9-50b4-8a37-a22c010e9338" "answer-ed13d739-9b67-541e-881c-81942c301938" "answer-c865c2be-4f2c-573a-8a7d-ef0e3fdb4dd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-447f87f9-dffa-5f29-8806-d225d659ee36" :answer/id #uuid "447f87f9-dffa-5f29-8806-d225d659ee36" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/03/0347d6a539b6e3288ff0939da134162ed95de9806e587323dda7052ca9496795.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e692f2d1-6ddc-5aa1-9d7c-917bbfff6ebb" :answer/id #uuid "e692f2d1-6ddc-5aa1-9d7c-917bbfff6ebb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/42/42e97d14f484c8236ff3a25dbed4c37310861dc9435237f8cd1311e4a8715812.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-622f3578-83a9-50b4-8a37-a22c010e9338" :answer/id #uuid "622f3578-83a9-50b4-8a37-a22c010e9338" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/59/59aa9eaaa095cbaf2289def489927888b278829c848b80c297203a030dfc4b62.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed13d739-9b67-541e-881c-81942c301938" :answer/id #uuid "ed13d739-9b67-541e-881c-81942c301938" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5c/5ce6940ee50ba454d351130eb65669407c81419db3a7b40c191c3100c8ba362e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c865c2be-4f2c-573a-8a7d-ef0e3fdb4dd1" :answer/id #uuid "c865c2be-4f2c-573a-8a7d-ef0e3fdb4dd1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9d/9db95cf46a9112d2f92e7ab9fe336b28d2da9c26971ba14360bdac772b6918e9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e1a27c07-b36b-5525-ba6b-847b13ebf516" :question/id #uuid "e1a27c07-b36b-5525-ba6b-847b13ebf516" :question/math-academy-id "q-213228" :question/problem "![](images/03/03ddf06402ad38708d232cf28783c817bf881965d54650eb158e7ffca4ea76a2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent irreflexive relations defined on the set $A={1,2,3}?$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be irreflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/b6/b63d99459e8271e70ec36fd417d67565f3d5e77316815d49c235468e174aa1e9.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to an irreflexive relation must not contain diagonal points. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-50c36a75-cd57-5a00-815a-7d34757ac50b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-50c36a75-cd57-5a00-815a-7d34757ac50b" :answer-field/id #uuid "50c36a75-cd57-5a00-815a-7d34757ac50b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a753fcea-864c-5d1d-9515-36b40da1b3f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bcc8cdb8-d4be-5768-99b5-0263aa670d03" "answer-a753fcea-864c-5d1d-9515-36b40da1b3f0" "answer-4c56e2bb-43ed-5906-85e4-b291c9d37ae8" "answer-9d2585bc-b01e-5f72-8bd0-21e0708314ed" "answer-003f486a-2600-584c-92ff-478adde52a81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcc8cdb8-d4be-5768-99b5-0263aa670d03" :answer/id #uuid "bcc8cdb8-d4be-5768-99b5-0263aa670d03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a753fcea-864c-5d1d-9515-36b40da1b3f0" :answer/id #uuid "a753fcea-864c-5d1d-9515-36b40da1b3f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c56e2bb-43ed-5906-85e4-b291c9d37ae8" :answer/id #uuid "4c56e2bb-43ed-5906-85e4-b291c9d37ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d2585bc-b01e-5f72-8bd0-21e0708314ed" :answer/id #uuid "9d2585bc-b01e-5f72-8bd0-21e0708314ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-003f486a-2600-584c-92ff-478adde52a81" :answer/id #uuid "003f486a-2600-584c-92ff-478adde52a81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204235 :question/problem "Which of the following digraphs represent a relation, defined on the set $A={1,2,3},$ that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nPairs of the form $(x,x)$ correspond to the loops that start and finish at the same node in the directed graphs.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflexive nor irreflexive, we require that some nodes (vertices) have a loop and some don't. Among the given options, only the following digraph has this property:\n\n![](images/84/847bcee3b9f9fc6672d5858111866141e043e390605cd92fb5579fd5193d7df4.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that nodes $1$ and $3$ have loops, while the node $2$ does not have a loop." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-62376fe5-0d16-504c-b19e-3a83d24ff291"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-62376fe5-0d16-504c-b19e-3a83d24ff291" :answer-field/id #uuid "62376fe5-0d16-504c-b19e-3a83d24ff291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" "answer-e4641094-b746-50c3-b042-2477f64a542e" "answer-52a9053f-f7fe-5c5a-8cb7-8caa90a4b936" "answer-d540945e-54e2-56f2-a282-982559d38faf" "answer-ab36a133-53cf-525b-b5f5-ae532b953a40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" :answer/id #uuid "0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/84/847bcee3b9f9fc6672d5858111866141e043e390605cd92fb5579fd5193d7df4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4641094-b746-50c3-b042-2477f64a542e" :answer/id #uuid "e4641094-b746-50c3-b042-2477f64a542e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/90/903c7d67b71386355439cb39a724c6be874ba4c7e3026343d91b429e649fac81.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52a9053f-f7fe-5c5a-8cb7-8caa90a4b936" :answer/id #uuid "52a9053f-f7fe-5c5a-8cb7-8caa90a4b936" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/95/95d0b20c7f11f2242c5e22ed8d66721cd8f0076ea5f0c8f0a996d8536fbd2a35.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d540945e-54e2-56f2-a282-982559d38faf" :answer/id #uuid "d540945e-54e2-56f2-a282-982559d38faf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cf/cf92336ff9f0a22f7ab5f30e3f3b336dab6f884b72a8deeccfdb00c3f926c5a7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab36a133-53cf-525b-b5f5-ae532b953a40" :answer/id #uuid "ab36a133-53cf-525b-b5f5-ae532b953a40" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/dd/ddfa6dfdf196e05ed653672d0e7c4369c75674e885d98b89abf1fdf0e4425474.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-653fba49-a6b9-5e57-b514-cf99f2424cd1" :question/id #uuid "653fba49-a6b9-5e57-b514-cf99f2424cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-213246" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive? \n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡2y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $y≡x+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(1,1)\\notin R$ since $1≢2(1)\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7),$ while\n\n- $(7,7)\\in R$ since $7≡2(7)\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≡x\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9)\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is irreflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\notin T$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≢x+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f7897328-67d4-5121-9241-5f901a3d93b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7897328-67d4-5121-9241-5f901a3d93b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7897328-67d4-5121-9241-5f901a3d93b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4de6a26-5382-5b6d-bf0e-07b0e5da5b96" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7295677-3fca-59ea-b647-9db4f20d343a" "answer-2e52c3bd-2b7a-5a24-95b6-a56a7a15447c" "answer-1ab03ed4-fb9b-5074-9880-fe1c53b1877b" "answer-b4de6a26-5382-5b6d-bf0e-07b0e5da5b96" "answer-d6c5b715-7c1c-5058-8ab1-617e85ee6cba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7295677-3fca-59ea-b647-9db4f20d343a" :answer/id #uuid "f7295677-3fca-59ea-b647-9db4f20d343a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ and $S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e52c3bd-2b7a-5a24-95b6-a56a7a15447c" :answer/id #uuid "2e52c3bd-2b7a-5a24-95b6-a56a7a15447c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ and $T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ab03ed4-fb9b-5074-9880-fe1c53b1877b" :answer/id #uuid "1ab03ed4-fb9b-5074-9880-fe1c53b1877b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ and $T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4de6a26-5382-5b6d-bf0e-07b0e5da5b96" :answer/id #uuid "b4de6a26-5382-5b6d-bf0e-07b0e5da5b96" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6c5b715-7c1c-5058-8ab1-617e85ee6cba" :answer/id #uuid "d6c5b715-7c1c-5058-8ab1-617e85ee6cba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7095468b-6aec-5ce6-83d1-ea12403a6b5a" :question/id #uuid "7095468b-6aec-5ce6-83d1-ea12403a6b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213240" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are reflexive? \n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x+y)∣10,$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $4∣({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y+1),$ defined on $Z$" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin R$ since $2+2=4$ and $4∤10,$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in R$ since $1+1=2$ and $2∣10.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\n4∣({x}^{2}-{x}^{2})\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin T$ since $2∤(2+1),$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in T$ since $1∣(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a904c1ac-f48c-541f-87b2-64440b6f4699"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a904c1ac-f48c-541f-87b2-64440b6f4699" :answer-field/id #uuid "a904c1ac-f48c-541f-87b2-64440b6f4699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58ae1950-b540-541c-bb35-734835ed6837" "answer-e7d8d161-c088-50a0-8cdb-b2dfab2b3cd6" "answer-a67c2cc7-31d2-5884-b5e7-bd42e8198442" "answer-21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" "answer-7c2cab9d-46e7-5fca-9e2e-839c1847e800"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58ae1950-b540-541c-bb35-734835ed6837" :answer/id #uuid "58ae1950-b540-541c-bb35-734835ed6837" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ and $T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7d8d161-c088-50a0-8cdb-b2dfab2b3cd6" :answer/id #uuid "e7d8d161-c088-50a0-8cdb-b2dfab2b3cd6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a67c2cc7-31d2-5884-b5e7-bd42e8198442" :answer/id #uuid "a67c2cc7-31d2-5884-b5e7-bd42e8198442" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ and $T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" :answer/id #uuid "21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c2cab9d-46e7-5fca-9e2e-839c1847e800" :answer/id #uuid "7c2cab9d-46e7-5fca-9e2e-839c1847e800" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cfc59310-e932-539a-95d8-99d9f3c66e0d" :question/id #uuid "cfc59310-e932-539a-95d8-99d9f3c66e0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-213245" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={1,3,5,7}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(1,3),(1,5),(3,5),(5,7)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on ${1,3,5,7},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R,\\,(5,5)\\notin R,\\,(7,7)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$ $\\text{for all }x\\in A,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80cb3597-f448-5b9b-8688-1a1dde9e0903" "answer-field-23232e55-2d25-5541-941b-dbcdf3cdf6e5" "answer-field-776fe9b3-0d9b-5b2e-a7ac-92cd899247f4" "answer-field-4300114a-f8a1-5bd4-8bd7-9ce4c6f28c11" "answer-field-ddd4f2c5-6ea0-54c5-a5b9-64c77f2c747b" "answer-field-cc14b513-043b-5977-90a5-64cfbbc74490" "answer-field-aa69c231-b7b0-5a10-bc54-20e6ad39f45f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80cb3597-f448-5b9b-8688-1a1dde9e0903" :answer-field/id #uuid "80cb3597-f448-5b9b-8688-1a1dde9e0903" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e17119af-369f-5ee9-b327-eea3cbee15b8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5dbeb5b2-6817-5ed7-8f59-a13edf34acf1" "answer-e17119af-369f-5ee9-b327-eea3cbee15b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dbeb5b2-6817-5ed7-8f59-a13edf34acf1" :answer/id #uuid "5dbeb5b2-6817-5ed7-8f59-a13edf34acf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\in " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e17119af-369f-5ee9-b327-eea3cbee15b8" :answer/id #uuid "e17119af-369f-5ee9-b327-eea3cbee15b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\notin " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-23232e55-2d25-5541-941b-dbcdf3cdf6e5" :answer