hoices ["answer-bc008276-7bc5-5a84-a02b-a9e55a47d2a2" "answer-028f1dfa-86c2-5e3a-a73a-1d56a9225107" "answer-5be97a4d-c3ce-551f-b557-328846a46e6c" "answer-1a81e9c1-7c28-5079-bc82-6430dce1e7cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc008276-7bc5-5a84-a02b-a9e55a47d2a2" :answer/id #uuid "bc008276-7bc5-5a84-a02b-a9e55a47d2a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-028f1dfa-86c2-5e3a-a73a-1d56a9225107" :answer/id #uuid "028f1dfa-86c2-5e3a-a73a-1d56a9225107" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5be97a4d-c3ce-551f-b557-328846a46e6c" :answer/id #uuid "5be97a4d-c3ce-551f-b557-328846a46e6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a81e9c1-7c28-5079-bc82-6430dce1e7cf" :answer/id #uuid "1a81e9c1-7c28-5079-bc82-6430dce1e7cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "reflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bcd445f-52b3-5de6-8b46-eb7aa3382e40" :question/id #uuid "2bcd445f-52b3-5de6-8b46-eb7aa3382e40" :question/math-academy-id "q-212140" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={0,1,2}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(0,0),(0,1),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on ${0,1,2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(0,0)\\in R,\\,(1,1)\\in R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(2,2)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(1,1)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fd502ea7-b1ea-5eaa-be81-70b834e4b3c7" "answer-field-68e80583-27f4-549f-817e-8eae51564802" "answer-field-b41293db-09e7-59d5-a63e-acb26cae819f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fd502ea7-b1ea-5eaa-be81-70b834e4b3c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd502ea7-b1ea-5eaa-be81-70b834e4b3c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3d6c50a1-6d85-5042-9e1d-f7f320f534bf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5105ed3-40e2-5038-b1d9-6e95da5b8b23" "answer-3d6c50a1-6d85-5042-9e1d-f7f320f534bf" "answer-b464ada9-c049-50e4-b6c5-7fd6ec4a9d1d" "answer-a370b2f4-4dcb-50e9-aa5e-c6d8cb3a8759"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5105ed3-40e2-5038-b1d9-6e95da5b8b23" :answer/id #uuid "f5105ed3-40e2-5038-b1d9-6e95da5b8b23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,2)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d6c50a1-6d85-5042-9e1d-f7f320f534bf" :answer/id #uuid "3d6c50a1-6d85-5042-9e1d-f7f320f534bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b464ada9-c049-50e4-b6c5-7fd6ec4a9d1d" :answer/id #uuid "b464ada9-c049-50e4-b6c5-7fd6ec4a9d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a370b2f4-4dcb-50e9-aa5e-c6d8cb3a8759" :answer/id #uuid "a370b2f4-4dcb-50e9-aa5e-c6d8cb3a8759" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68e80583-27f4-549f-817e-8eae51564802" :answer-field/id #uuid "68e80583-27f4-549f-817e-8eae51564802" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-72067d41-59b5-592f-b53b-26438318bb9d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72067d41-59b5-592f-b53b-26438318bb9d" "answer-a1e3c218-5ca8-56ad-ae43-4156862f278d" "answer-7ff805be-2c