 $(♢,♡)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72c8a633-4dde-55ab-9fee-4b1ced22ca41" :answer/id #uuid "72c8a633-4dde-55ab-9fee-4b1ced22ca41" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "for all $x\\in A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5a923e7-2a04-5c6e-a603-d254b35c1171" :answer/id #uuid "a5a923e7-2a04-5c6e-a603-d254b35c1171" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "for some $x\\in A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d7731e6-68a6-52ce-a6e4-1ee9c5d23ced" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7731e6-68a6-52ce-a6e4-1ee9c5d23ced" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-fa10a46b-a0fa-5719-90e0-0cf86e6b7dac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa10a46b-a0fa-5719-90e0-0cf86e6b7dac" "answer-f2ba276c-d015-5725-8277-b0b5827c6528" "answer-c6cd7d42-d8fe-5432-9a66-7fce567e6b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa10a46b-a0fa-5719-90e0-0cf86e6b7dac" :answer/id #uuid "fa10a46b-a0fa-5719-90e0-0cf86e6b7dac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2ba276c-d015-5725-8277-b0b5827c6528" :answer/id #uuid "f2ba276c-d015-5725-8277-b0b5827c6528" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6cd7d42-d8fe-5432-9a66-7fce567e6b2c" :answer/id #uuid "c6cd7d42-d8fe-5432-9a66-7fce567e6b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "reflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ccf91b35-7753-51f7-9fcf-6efffb54e68e" :question/id #uuid "ccf91b35-7753-51f7-9fcf-6efffb54e68e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213202" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $2∤(y-x)$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nThe relation $R$ is irreflexive. Indeed, since $2∣(x-x)$ for all $x\\in Z,$ we have $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$  $\\text{ for all }x\\in Z,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-953a509c-0254-5c7a-82f3-a3fdb97787bf" "answer-field-21daace1-64ff-5ce7-897b-c4554c1fd8c6" "answer-field-9778012a-e1b1-578f-b273-4592e36ba105"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-953a509c-0254-5c7a-82f3-a3fdb97787bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "953a509c-0254-5c7a-82f3-a3fdb97787bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-792a0ee2-6925-501e-9e31-987367dde6bc" "answer-76db6319-13a0-5813-bfe7-3b42914cb5da" "answer-6cac4573-0da4-5a5f-b13e-cacab51aa082" "answer-104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-792a0ee2-6925-501e-9e31-987367dde6bc" :answer/id #uuid "792a0ee2-6925-501e-9e31-987367dde6bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76db6319-13a0-5813-bfe7-3b42914cb5da" :answer/id #uuid "76db6319-13a0-5813-bfe7-3b42914cb5da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,5)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cac4573-0da4-5a5f-b13e-cacab51aa082" :answer/id #uuid "6cac4573-0da4-5a5f-b13e-cacab51aa082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77" :answer/id #uuid "104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-21daace1-64ff-5ce7-897b-c4554c1fd8c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "21daace1-64ff-5ce7-897b-c4554c1fd8c6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-59eb980b-caf6-54f9-a10c-5793952ad04d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19832d4c-4f38-57f7-bb47-2e4d78cada0f" "answer-b8bbc85b-78bb-5ac5-905b-34d5facbf724" "answer-59eb980b-caf6-54f9-a10c-5793952ad04d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19832d4c-4f38-57f7-bb47-2e4d78cada0f" :answer/id #uuid "19832d4c-4f38-57f7-bb47-2e4d78cada0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and $(2,2)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8bbc85b-78bb-5ac5-905b-34d5facbf724" :answer/id #uuid "b8bbc85b-78bb-5ac5-905b-34d5facbf724" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and $(5,5)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59eb980b-caf6-54f9-a10c-5793952ad04d" :answer/id #uuid "59eb980b-caf6-54f9-a10c-5793952ad04d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "for all $x\\in Z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9778012a-e1b1-578f-b273-4592e36ba105" :answer-field/id #uuid "9778012a-e1b1-578f-b273-4592e36ba105" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-95b90f36-d02a-51d7-95b7-b61a1fa42298" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7dd4966d-f600-50e1-85d7-6229bee89aff" "answer-95b90f36-d02a-51d7-95b7-b61a1fa42298" "answer-47a850bc-ccb2-5cfe-9773-c5fe2f42616e" "answer-8a4da341-9ee6-5cf4-88ac-dd701d3d9a39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dd4966d-f600-50e1-85d7-6229bee89aff" :answer/id #uuid "7dd4966d-f600-50e1-85d7-6229bee89aff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95b90f36-d02a-51d7-95b7-b61a1fa42298" :answer/id #uuid "95b90f36-d02a-51d7-95b7-b61a1fa42298" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47a850bc-ccb2-5cfe-9773-c5fe2f42616e" :answer/id #uuid "47a850bc-ccb2-5cfe-9773-c5fe2f42616e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a4da341-9ee6-5cf4-88ac-dd701d3d9a39" :answer/id #uuid "8a4da341-9ee6-5cf4-88ac-dd701d3d9a39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "reflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204236 :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x-{y}^{2}=0$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(-1,-1)\\notin R$ since the pair does not satisfy the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n(-1)-(-1)^{2}=-2\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- $(0,0)\\in R$ since the pair satisfies the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n(0)-(0)^{2}=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(-1,-1)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(0,0)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37f15f8e-9c05-53c1-b593-9246c68b848e" "answer-field-47fe7fb7-8e8a-54d9-8d2f-6039eeb4bf9a" "answer-field-a273d003-dffb-5811-a5d8-4b681c5e1492"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37f15f8e-9c05-53c1-b593-9246c68b848e" :answer-field/id #uuid "37f15f8e-9c05-53c1-b593-9246c68b848e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-495c688c-9c79-5650-becd-e720994fe31f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-495c688c-9c79-5650-becd-e720994fe31f" "answer-9fea72e1-ea24-5b0c-b646-d5398d396939" "answer-f7d0153e-a37f-5f88-a02f-701762bb86d6" "answer-14634958-496e-54f5-b885-eeae73164e08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-495c688c-9c79-5650-becd-e720994fe31f" :answer/id #uuid "495c688c-9c79-5650-becd-e720994fe31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-1)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fea72e1-ea24-5b0c-b646-d5398d396939" :answer/id #uuid "9fea72e1-ea24-5b0c-b646-d5398d396939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7d0153e-a37f-5f88-a02f-701762bb86d6" :answer/id #uuid "f7d0153e-a37f-5f88-a02f-701762bb86d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14634958-496e-54f5-b885-eeae73164e08" :answer/id #uuid "14634958-496e-54f5-b885-eeae73164e08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-47fe7fb7-8e8a-54d9-8d2f-6039eeb4bf9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "47fe7fb7-8e8a-54d9-8d2f-6039eeb4bf9a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9e02b9af-6a66-53ce-b5ca-b2973651bd29" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9db9a487-357d-5053-b70e-61ed92cb1178" "answer-9e02b9af-6a66-53ce-b5ca-b2973651bd29" "answer-f9637fc7-5b65-5648-bffc-c57c0e38a6d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9db9a487-357d-5053-b70e-61ed92cb1178" :answer/id #uuid "9db9a487-357d-5053-b70e-61ed92cb1178" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and $(-1,-1)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e02b9af-6a66-53ce-b5ca-b2973651bd29" :answer/id #uuid "9e02b9af-6a66-53ce-b5ca-b2973651bd29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and $(0,0)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9637fc7-5b65-5648-bffc-c57c0e38a6d0" :answer/id #uuid "f9637fc7-5b65-5648-bffc-c57c0e38a6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "for all $x\\in A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a273d003-dffb-5811-a5d8-4b681c5e1492" :answer-field/id #uuid "a273d003-dffb-5811-a5d8-4b681c5e1492" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-473beea7-931e-5978-a041-ecf4a6d95c35" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2ee89c1-f421-512a-b6dd-9a79b8d20f3b" "answer-306872e7-1d7b-5d08-a4d5-765ca66562d0" "answer-473beea7-931e-5978-a041-ecf4a6d95c35" "answer-34f96acd-fc2a-53e4-af03-f1157ecff40d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2ee89c1-f421-512a-b6dd-9a79b8d20f3b" :answer/id #uuid "b2ee89c1-f421-512a-b6dd-9a79b8d20f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-306872e7-1d7b-5d08-a4d5-765ca66562d0" :answer/id #uuid "306872e7-1d7b-5d08-a4d5-765ca66562d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-473beea7-931e-5978-a041-ecf4a6d95c35" :answer/id #uuid "473beea7-931e-5978-a041-ecf4a6d95c35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34f96acd-fc2a-53e4-af03-f1157ecff40d" :answer/id #uuid "34f96acd-fc2a-53e4-af03-f1157ecff40d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "reflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c3deb4f-bd86-5557-b5a7-4c0dc0f448ab" :question/id #uuid "8c3deb4f-bd86-5557-b5a7-4c0dc0f448ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-213201" :question/problem "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $R$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $y-{x}^{3}\\ne 0$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(1,1)\\notin R$ since the pair does not satisfy the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n1-{1}^{3}=0\n$$\n\n- $(2,2)\\in R$ since the pair satisfies the underlying condition:\n\n$$\n2-{2}^{3}=-6\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(1,1)\\notin R$ $\\text{and }(2,2)\\in R,$ the relation is $\\text{neither reflexive nor irreflexive}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb9fad6c-7818-5c2d-a769-230889739a42" "answer-field-2e604926-3a36-5408-9f7c-7bb120698a05" "answer-field-69fa6a06-e016-5c5c-be5a-48734df01714"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb9fad6c-7818-5c2d-a769-230889739a42" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb9fad6c-7818-5c2d-a769-230889739a42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9f2553b4-156d-5655-8e80-de4eda022fa2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f2553b4-156d-5655-8e80-de4eda022fa2" "answer-78d5ecdf-122b-58eb-ac26-5fed89e25521" "answer-d5e953b4-d42b-51c2-96f3-22437543b47d" "answer-2129ea14-351e-5487-85a4-c62570378b81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f2553b4-156d-5655-8e80-de4eda022fa2" :answer/id #uuid "9f2553b4-156d-5655-8e80-de4eda022fa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,1)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78d5ecdf-122b-58eb-ac26-5fed89e25521" :answer/id #uuid "78d5ecdf-122b-58eb-ac26-5fed89e25521" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,2)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5e953b4-d42b-51c2-96f3-22437543b47d" :answer/id #uuid "d5e953b4-d42b-51c2-96f3-22437543b47d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2129ea14-351e-5487-85a4-c62570378b81" :answer/id #uuid "2129ea14-351e-5487-85a4-c62570378b81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x,x)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e604926-3a36-5408-9f7c-7bb120698a05" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e604926-3a36-5408-9f7c-7bb120698a05" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bba561ba-b6af-55b0-ae72-0463a4b72f2c" "answer-0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" "answer-204ca137-4335-5470-825e-0717b79cf8e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bba561ba-b6af-55b0-ae72-0463a4b72f2c" :answer/id #uuid "bba561ba-b6af-55b0-ae72-0463a4b72f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and $(1,1)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" :answer/id #uuid "0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "and $(2,2)\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-204ca137-4335-5470-825e-0717b79cf8e0" :answer/id #uuid "204ca137-4335-5470-825e-0717b79cf8e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "for all $x\\in R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69fa6a06-e016-5c5c-be5a-48734df01714" :answer-field/id #uuid "69fa6a06-e016-5c5c-be5a-48734df01714" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-cf5cae6a-e729-53e2-88b5-5a9de238ea8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-93e18950-29a8-52a9-b857-947d72ceb229" "answer-feafc819-cf17-5297-8433-9423e52907b5" "answer-cf5cae6a-e729-53e2-88b5-5a9de238ea8a" "answer-a3afeb18-144e-59cc-aabf-0cce033183ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93e18950-29a8-52a9-b857-947d72ceb229" :answer/id #uuid "93e18950-29a8-52a9-b857-947d72ceb229" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "both reflexive and irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-feafc819-cf17-5297-8433-9423e52907b5" :answer/id #uuid "feafc819-cf17-5297-8433-9423e52907b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf5cae6a-e729-53e2-88b5-5a9de238ea8a" :answer/id #uuid "cf5cae6a-e729-53e2-88b5-5a9de238ea8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "neither reflexive nor irreflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3afeb18-144e-59cc-aabf-0cce033183ad" :answer/id #uuid "a3afeb18-144e-59cc-aabf-0cce033183ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "reflexive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205233 :tutorial/content "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is called **reflexive** if $(x,x) \\in R$ for every element $x \\in A.$ In other words, each element of $A$ is related to itself by $R.$\n\nFor example:\n\n- Any integer $x$ is congruent to itself modulo $n$ for any natural $n.$\n\n$$\nx\\equiv x \\quad(\\textrm{mod } n)\n$$\n\nSo, congruence of integers is reflexive.\n\n- The relation \"are born in the same year,\" defined on the set containing the entire human population, is also reflexive. This is because any person was born in the same year as themselves.\n\nA binary relation $R$ on a set $A$ is called **irreflexive** if $(x,x) \\notin R$ for every element $x \\in A.$ In other words, no element of $A$ is related to itself by $R.$\n\nFor example:\n\n- The relation \"is less than\" $(\\lt),$ defined on the set of real numbers, is irreflexive since no number is less than itself. In other words, the statement\n\n$$\nx < x\n$$\n\nis *false* for any $x\\in\\mathbb R.$\n\n- The relation \"is the sisters of,\" defined on the set containing all people, is irreflexive. This is because a person can't be their own sister.\n\nA relation *cannot* be both reflexive and irreflexive simultaneously. However, most relations are neither reflexive nor irreflexive. \n\nFor example, consider relation $x \\: R \\: y,$ defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$ as $xy \\lt 10{:}$ \n\n- $R$ is not reflexive since $5 \\cdot 5 \\not\\lt 10,$ which means that $5$ is not related to itself.\n\n- $R$ is not irreflexive since $1 \\cdot 1 \\lt 10,$ which means that $1$ is related to itself.\n\nWe can summarize all the above in the following diagram:\n\n![](images/f6/f60867376793fc07fce1dd398e00a0c6fd3051cce95ee98f1fe48b843dab4539.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205245 :tutorial/content "Let's describe the properties of adjacency matrices for reflexive and irreflexive relations.\n\n- A finite binary relation is reflexive if and only if its adjacency matrix has only $1$'s on the main diagonal (from top-left to bottom-right). \n\nFor example, the relation $R = \\big\\{ (1,1), (1,2), (2,2), (3,3) \\big\\},$ defined on $\\{1,2,3\\},$ is reflexive, and its adjacency matrix is the following:\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $0$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |\n\n- A finite binary relation is irreflexive if and only if its adjacency matrix has only $0$'s on the main diagonal. \n\nFor example, the relation $R = \\big\\{ (1,2), (1,3), (2,1), (3,1), (3,2) \\big\\},$ defined on $\\{1,2,3\\},$ is irreflexive, and its adjacency matrix is the following:\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |\n\nFor relations that are neither reflexive nor irreflexive, the corresponding adjacency matrix will have both $0$'s and $1$'s on the main diagonal." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205244 :tutorial/content "Plots of reflexive and irreflexive relations have the following properties:\n\n- A binary relation is reflexive if and only if its plot contains all the corresponding points on the line $y=x.$ \n\nFor example, the relation $R = \\big\\{ (1,1), (1,2), (2,2), (3,3) \\big\\},$ defined on $\\{1,2,3\\},$ is reflexive, and its plot contains all the diagonal points, as shown below:\n\n![](images/2c/2c7f9c6eb18ca50f58a9f214c31ab3d80e6fd652f048f3502aafc06e7e330687.png)\n\n \n\n- A binary relation is irreflexive if and only if its plot does *not* contain *any* points on the line $y=x.$ \n\nFor example, the relation $R = \\big\\{ (1,2), (1,3), (2,1), (3,1), (3,2) \\big\\},$ defined on $\\{1,2,3\\},$ is irreflexive, and its plot does not contain *any* diagonal points, as shown below:\n\n![](images/33/33d033652c69df776b911c742c6f8f81b0c4bba81c50bf5aba2118877ed75c73.png)\n\n \n\nFor relations that are neither reflexive nor irreflexive, the corresponding plot will have some points on the line $y=x$ but not all of them." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186205246 :tutorial/content "Digraphs of reflexive and irreflexive relations have the following properties:\n\n- A binary relation is reflexive if and only if its digraph has a loop at every node. \n\nFor example, the relation $R = \\big\\{ (1,1), (1,2), (2,2), (3,3) \\big\\},$ defined on $\\{1,2,3\\},$ is reflexive, and its digraph has a loop at each node, as shown below:\n\n![](images/8b/8b4b6d97ba6901b72fbde16bc992887ed9db05cd3b522c1899a177070a2afe38.png)\n\n \n\n- A binary relation is irreflexive if and only if its digraph does *not* contain *any* loops at the nodes. \n\nFor example, the relation $R = \\big\\{ (1,2), (1,3), (2,1), (3,1), (3,2) \\big\\},$ defined on $\\{1,2,3\\},$ is irreflexive, and its digraph has no loops, as shown below:\n\n![](images/43/432e41e141ecdcd95b6f1bbe6e94a411751806b48675c2eca98a9d625e94d4f1.png)\n\n \n\nFor relations that are neither reflexive nor irreflexive, the corresponding digraph will have loops at some nodes but not at all of them." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204112 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
